══ FRICTION LOG ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1. STEP MATHEMATICS
   A fraction only builds up when BOTH parts are numbers — `rise/run` stays a slash
   evidence: "_m_ = rise/run" painted as "<i>m</i> = rise/run"
   costs:    the author has to know the fraction grammar is numeric, and rewrite the idea or accept a slash

2. DRAWING A STRAIGHT LINE
   The object called "line" cannot draw a straight line — it is axis-parallel only, so a sloping line has to be entered as a "function"
   evidence: the graph offers [function, line, points, segment]; "line" takes y = k or x = k, so _y_ = 2_x_ − 1 must be typed as the function "2x-1"
   costs:    in a lesson ABOUT straight lines, the control named line is the wrong one every single time

3. TYPOGRAPHY OF THE FIGURE
   The axis numbering uses a hyphen where the lesson's own text uses a minus sign
   evidence: 11 axis labels begin with "-" and 0 with "−", on a page whose prose and working are written with − throughout
   costs:    the same number is set two ways on one screen

